      ":question/worked-solution": "Let's attempt to solve each equation in turn:\n\n- For the first equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x-9 & =-x-9 \\\\ -x-9+x & =-x-9+x \\\\ -9 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-x-9=-x-9$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the second equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x-2 & =-4x-2 \\\\ -4x-2+4x & =-4x-2+4x \\\\ -2 & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is true for all values of $x.$ Therefore, the equation $-4x-2=-4x-2$ has infinitely many solutions.\n\n- For the third equation, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-x+9 & =-x-9 \\\\ -x+9+x & =-x-9+x \\\\ 9 & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation is false for all values of $x.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $-x-9=-x-9$; $-4x-2=-4x-2$ only.",
